            <ArticleTitle>Persistent müllerian duct syndrome with torsion of an intra-abdominal seminoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>256-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Persistent Müllerian Duct Syndrome (PMDS) is a particular form of male pseudohermaphroditism. Due to the absence or inactivity of Müllerian Inhibiting Substance (MIS), no regression is observed of the Müllerian ducts in a genotypical and phenotypical male individual. This leads to the development of fallopian tubes, uterus and proximal vagina. The testes often lie intra-abdominally and are exposed to malignant degeneration. A case is described in which the diagnosis of PMDS was made by laparotomy for an acute abdomen, caused by torsion of a seminoma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
